## Scenario

A Node.js application needs to implement a robust task scheduler that makes periodic asynchronous API calls to fetch data from an external service. The application must perform a computation on the retrieved data and handle various failure scenarios gracefully. 

The scheduler should execute this task every hour and enforce a strict 5-second timeout constraint on each API call. If the API call exceeds this timeout, the operation must be terminated and an error should be logged without crashing the application. The implementation should also handle network errors, invalid responses, and ensure that failed tasks do not prevent subsequent scheduled executions.

Additionally, the task scheduler must be able to gracefully shut down, canceling any pending operations and cleaning up resources properly.

## Question

