You are building a React component that needs to dynamically apply a CSS class to an element based on a boolean state variable. The component should display a button that toggles between two visual states: "active" and "inactive". When the user clicks the button, the state changes and the corresponding class should be applied to a div element.

## Question

Which of the following code snippets can be used to dynamically add a class to an element based on a state variable in React?

## Options

A) 
```javascript
const [isActive, setIsActive] = useState(false);
return <div className={isActive ? 'active' : 'inactive'}>Content</div>;
```

B)
```javascript
const [isActive, setIsActive] = useState(false);
return <div class={isActive && 'active'}>Content</div>;
```

C)
```javascript
const [isActive, setIsActive] = useState(false);
return <div className={`${isActive ? 'active' : ''} base-class`}>Content</div>;
```

D)
```javascript
const [isActive, setIsActive] = useState(false);
const element = document.getElementById('myDiv');
element.classList.add(isActive ? 'active' : 'inactive');
return <div id="myDiv">Content</div>;
```

E)
```javascript
const [isActive, setIsActive] = useState(false);
return <div className={isActive && 'active' ? 'active' : 'inactive'}>Content</div>;
```

