# Angular: BTC to USD

## Scenario

You are working on a financial dashboard application built with Angular. The application needs to display Bitcoin prices converted to USD in multiple locations throughout the templates. To avoid code duplication and maintain consistency, you decide to implement a custom pipe that leverages an existing `BitcoinService` to fetch the current BTC to USD conversion rate.

The `BitcoinService` has already been created with the following method:
```
getExchangeRate(): Observable<number>
```

This method returns an Observable that emits the current Bitcoin to USD exchange rate. You need to create a custom pipe named `BtcToUsd` that accepts a Bitcoin amount as input and transforms it to its USD equivalent by multiplying it by the exchange rate from the service.

Your pipe will be used in templates like:
```
{{ 2.5 | btcToUsd }}
```

## Question

Which of the following implementations correctly creates a custom pipe that transforms Bitcoin values to USD using the injected BitcoinService?

A) 
```typescript
@Pipe({ name: 'btcToUsd' })
export class BtcToUsdPipe implements PipeTransform {
  constructor(private bitcoinService: BitcoinService) {}

  transform(value: number): number {
    let rate = 0;
    this.bitcoinService.getExchangeRate().subscribe(r => rate = r);
    return value * rate;
  }
}
```

B)
```typescript
@Pipe({ name: 'btcToUsd' })
export class BtcToUsdPipe implements PipeTransform {
  constructor(private bitcoinService: BitcoinService) {}

  transform(value: number): Observable<number> {
    return this.bitcoinService.getExchangeRate().pipe(
      map(rate => value * rate)
    );
  }
}
```

C)
```typescript
@Pipe({ name: 'btcToUsd' })
export class BtcToUsdPipe implements PipeTransform {
  exchangeRate: number = 0;

  constructor(private bitcoinService: BitcoinService) {
    this.bitcoinService.getExchangeRate().subscribe(
      rate => this.exchangeRate = rate
    );
  }

  transform(value: number): number {
    return value * this.exchangeRate;
  }
}
```

D)
```typescript
@Pipe({ name: 'btcToUsd' })
export class BtcToUsdPipe implements PipeTransform {
  constructor(private bitcoinService: BitcoinService) {}

  transform(value: number): Observable<number> {
    return this.bitcoinService.getExchangeRate().pipe(
      map(rate => value * rate),
      shareReplay(1)
    );
  }
}
```

