# Code Review: Toggle View Hook

You are reviewing the implementation of the "Enhanced View Mode Persistence" feature for a travel app's dashboard. The feature allows users to toggle between different view modes (List, Grid, Map) and persists their preference using localStorage.

Below is the current implementation:

```javascript
import React, { useState, useEffect } from 'react';

const ViewModeToggle = () => {
  const [viewMode, setViewMode] = useState('list');
  const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(true);

  useEffect(() => {
    const savedMode = localStorage.getItem('viewMode');
    if (savedMode) {
      setViewMode(savedMode);
    }
    setIsLoading(false);
  });

  const handleToggle = (mode) => {
    setViewMode(mode);
    localStorage.setItem('viewMode', mode);
  };

  if (isLoading) {
    return <div>Loading...</div>;
  }

  return (
    <div className="toggle-container">
      <button onClick={() => handleToggle('list')} 
              className={viewMode === 'list' ? 'active' : ''}>
        List View
      </button>
      <button onClick={() => handleToggle('grid')} 
              className={viewMode === 'grid' ? 'active' : ''}>
        Grid View
      </button>
      <button onClick={() => handleToggle('map')} 
              className={viewMode === 'map' ? 'active' : ''}>
        Map View
      </button>
      <div className="content">
        {viewMode === 'list' && <ListView />}
        {viewMode === 'grid' && <GridView />}
        {viewMode === 'map' && <MapView />}
      </div>
    </div>
  );
};

export default ViewModeToggle;
```

